# What must never enter a build context.
#
# Read this as two lists. The first is about SECRETS and is the reason this
# file is not optional: anything left in the context can be `COPY`d by a later
# edit to the Dockerfile, and anything in a layer is in the image even if a
# subsequent layer deletes it. The second is about SIZE, and is why `docker
# build` from this repository takes seconds rather than minutes -- `web/
# node_modules` alone is larger than every source file in the project put
# together.
#
# Verify rather than trust. From the repository root:
#
#   docker build -t recon-api .
#   docker run --rm --entrypoint sh recon-api -c 'ls -a /app'
#
# There must be no `.env` in that listing, and none anywhere in the image:
#
#   docker run --rm --entrypoint sh recon-api -c 'find / -name ".env" 2>/dev/null'

# --- secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.env` is the one file in this repository that holds live credentials. It is
# gitignored; it must also be dockerignored, because a build context is not a
# git checkout and .gitignore has no effect on it.
#
# There is deliberately NO `!.env.example` re-inclusion here. The example file
# holds no secrets, but a negation on a `.env*` pattern is exactly the kind of
# line that gets widened later, and the image has no use for it.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.env.local
**/.env.production.local
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# --- runtime state, never baked into an image ---------------------------------
# `out/` holds the SQLite database, generated datasets and the upload blob
# store. In a deployment these live on a mounted volume; a copy baked into the
# image would be a stale database that shadows the volume on first boot and a
# set of somebody else's uploaded files shipped inside the artefact.
out/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- generated fixtures -------------------------------------------------------
# 1.7 MB, uncommitted, and regenerable from the seed. The API does not read it;
# only `tests/test_scale_acceptance.py` does, and tests are not in the image.
fixtures/seed42-5000/

# --- language toolchain caches ------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- the console ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The web app is deployed by Vercel from the git repository, not from this
# image. `web/node_modules` is the single largest directory in the tree.
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
node_modules/
.next/

# --- version control and tooling ----------------------------------------------
# `.git` carries every past revision of every file, including anything that was
# ever committed and later removed.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.claude/
.superpowers/
.remember/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- not needed at runtime ----------------------------------------------------
tests/
bench/
docs/
deploy/
*.md
!README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
